  "claim": "This actor appeared in Bolexbrothers second feature film, a 2005 French-British computer-animated adventure fantasy that was based on a TV series. He also starred in the film Sexy Beast,",
  "evidencia": "Page: Ray Winstone. Sentence: He has appeared in films such as \"Cold Mountain\", \"Nil By Mouth\", \"King Arthur\", \"The Magic Roundabout\", \"The Departed\", \"Beowulf\", \"Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull\", \"Edge of Darkness\", \"The Sweeney\" and \"Noah\".\nPage: The Magic Roundabout (film). Sentence: The Magic Roundabout (released in France as Pollux - Le manège enchanté and redubbed in the United States as Doogal or The Lord of the Springs) is a 2005 French-British computer-animated adventure fantasy film based on the television series \"The Magic Roundabout\".\nPage: Sexy Beast. Sentence: The film stars Ray Winstone, Ben Kingsley and Ian McShane.\nPage: Bolexbrothers. Sentence: The studio specialises in stop motion animation, producing numerous short films and commercials, as well as one stop motion feature film, \"The Secret Adventures of Tom Thumb\" (their second feature, \"The Magic Roundabout\", was computer animated).",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Ray Winstone. Sentence: He has appeared in films such as \"Cold Mountain\", \"Nil By Mouth\", \"King Arthur\", \"The Magic Roundabout\", \"The Departed\", \"Beowulf\", \"Indiana Jones and the Kingdom of the Crystal Skull\", \"Edge of Darkness\", \"The Sweeney\" and \"Noah\".\nPage: The Magic Roundabout (film). Sentence: The Magic Roundabout (released in France as Pollux - Le manège enchanté and redubbed in the United States as Doogal or The Lord of the Springs) is a 2005 French-British computer-animated adventure fantasy film based on the television series \"The Magic Roundabout\".\nPage: Sexy Beast. Sentence: The film stars Ray Winstone, Ben Kingsley and Ian McShane.\nPage: Bolexbrothers. Sentence: The studio specialises in stop motion animation, producing numerous short films and commercials, as well as one stop motion feature film, \"The Secret Adventures of Tom Thumb\" (their second feature, \"The Magic Roundabout\", was computer animated).",
